<p>Most property claims start with an estimate written after a single inspection, often before anything has been opened up. Then the roofer tears off the shingles and finds soft decking, or the water mitigation crew pulls baseboards and finds wet framing two rooms away. <strong>Insurance claim supplements in San Antonio</strong> are how that new information gets back to the insurer. A supplement asks the carrier to revise the estimate for damage or items that were missed, measured short, or impossible to see the first time. Done well, it is specific, documented, and easy for the insurer to review.</p>

